  "answer": "sandbox6283 is AWS account 930416275108 (owner dvarga).\n\n**ci-runner is no longer an IAM user in this account.** list_users returns only ci-runner-ro and svc-backup. That does not mean it never existed. CloudTrail still has its history:\n\n| UTC | event | by |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-09-20 22:41:05 | CreateAccessKey (iam) | ci-runner |\n| 2026-09-21 03:14:07 | RunInstances (ec2) | ci-runner |\n| 2026-09-21 03:14:31 | CreateTags (ec2) | ci-runner |\n| 2026-09-22 09:02:31 | DeleteAccessKey (iam) | kfarrow |\n| 2026-09-22 09:02:44 | DeleteUser (iam) | kfarrow |\n\nSo ci-runner created an access key on 2026-09-20, and on 2026-09-22 kfarrow ran DeleteAccessKey and then DeleteUser 13 seconds apart. That sequence is consistent with removing ci-runner's key and the user itself. The SQL columns don't show the target of those calls, so I can't confirm that from CloudTrail alone.\n\n**Does it still have an active key?** I can't tell from these tools. With the user gone from IAM there is no key list to read, so its key status cannot be confirmed either way. Don't confuse it with ci-runner-ro, a different user whose key AKIA7QK2M4X9CRRO0001 is Active.\n\n**Is anything it launched still running in eu-west-3?** Yes. i-05d2c8e71a94f3b60 is a c6i.8xlarge in eu-west-3b, launched 2026-09-21T03:14:09Z (two seconds after ci-runner's RunInstances), and still running. It is tagged Name=perf-burst-runner-07, pipeline=nightly-perf, with public IP 198.51.100.73. Deleting the user did not stop it, so it is still costing money. The only other eu-west-3 instance, i-0b71f4a93c2e6d508 (perf-jump-host, t3.small), predates ci-runner's activity.\n"
